    sh:description "A Calculation Profile, is an abstract parent of calculation-method profiles that fixes the method, parameters, and assumptions used to compute a risk measure, used as the generic semantic core so that a specific method is one concrete profile rather than the only universal calculation path. It is bound to a RiskMeasureSpecification and points at an ImplementationVersion for reproducibility.";
